#Where a peptide bond may be attacked, and from which direction the attack
#counts. Read by peptidebond.sites.
#
#Format: <resname> <type> <antecedent> [[~|^]<plane>[:angle]]
#
#ATOMS ARE NAMED BY THEIR GROUP, the first column of the .grp -- MC for
#methionine's carbonyl carbon, MO for its oxygen. That is the name a reduced
#topology carries, so there is one convention and nothing to translate.
#
#THE ELECTROPHILE, '<RES> <C> <O> ^<CA>:75'
#
#  the carbonyl carbon is what gets attacked; its oxygen is the antecedent, so
#  the base direction is OPPOSITE C=O; and '^' puts the two directions out of
#  the (C, O, CA) plane, one on each face, tilted 75 degrees off that base --
#  which is 105 degrees from the C=O axis. That is where the carbonyl's pi*
#  lobe is, and a nucleophile arriving anywhere else does not reach it (Burgi &
#  Dunitz, 1974). The ribosome's own pre-attack state, 1VY4, measures 100.6
#  degrees at 3.204 A.
#
#THE NUCLEOPHILE, '<RES> <N> <CA>'
#
#  the attacking nitrogen, and its only heavy neighbour, so its lone pair
#  points away from CA -- which is the direction it attacks along. No plane and
#  no '-C': a nitrogen that can attack is a free terminus by construction
#  (PeptideBondFormation::_isFree refuses one already bonded to another
#  residue's carbonyl), so CA is all it has.
#
#BOTH ENDS HAVE TO BE HERE. This file, when given, is the only table the
#peptide bond term reads; it does not fall back to the .hbond for a half it is
#missing. The angular factor is applied per end and SKIPPED when a site is
#absent, so a half-filled table makes a bond form MORE readily, not less.
#
#A residue not named here simply has no site, which the run reports. Add one by
#giving it the same columns.

#The electrophiles.

ALA  AC     AO     ^ACA:75
ARG  RC     RO     ^RCA:75
ASN  NC     NO     ^NCA:75
ASP  DC     DO     ^DCA:75
CYS  CC     CO     ^CCA:75
GLN  QC     QO     ^QCA:75
GLU  EC     EO     ^ECA:75
GLY  GC     GO     ^GCA:75
HIS  HC     HO     ^HCA:75
ILE  IC     IO     ^ICA:75
LEU  LC     LO     ^LCA:75
LYS  KC     KO     ^KCA:75
MET  MC     MO     ^MCA:75
PHE  FC     FO     ^FCA:75
PRO  PC     PO     ^PCA:75
SER  SC     SO     ^SCA:75
THR  TC     TO     ^TCA:75
TRP  WC     WO     ^WCA:75
TYR  YC     YO     ^YCA:75
VAL  VC     VO     ^VCA:75

#The nucleophiles.

ALA  AN     ACA
ARG  RN     RCA
ASN  NN     NCA
ASP  DN     DCA
CYS  CN     CCA
GLN  QN     QCA
GLU  EN     ECA
GLY  GN     GCA
HIS  HN     HCA
ILE  IN     ICA
LEU  LN     LCA
LYS  KN     KCA
MET  MN     MCA
PHE  FN     FCA
PRO  PN     PCA
SER  SN     SCA
THR  TN     TCA
TRP  WN     WCA
TYR  YN     YCA
VAL  VN     VCA
